WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.440
The saga of the planet Mandalore is spread&nbsp;
across '90s comic book series Tales of the Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.640
the animated series The Clone&nbsp;
Wars and Star Wars Rebels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.360
and the live-action series The Mandalorian.&nbsp;
Here is the history of Mandalore explained.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.000
After the runaway success of&nbsp;
the original Star Wars in 1977,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.200
the future was wide open for sequel The Empire&nbsp;
Strikes Back. Among the many abandoned concepts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.720
for the second part of the original trilogy was an&nbsp;
army of Imperial Super Troopers, armored badasses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:34.160
from the Mandalore system. As conceived by George&nbsp;
Lucas and designed by visual effects supervisor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.440
Joe Johnston and concept artist Ralph McQuarrie,&nbsp;
the Super Troopers would have an ancient grudge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.840
against the Jedi and an array of weapons&nbsp;
integrated into their suits to combat them.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.160
These concepts would end up forming the basis&nbsp;
of Mandalorians as we know them much later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.600
but at the time, the budget simply didn't exist&nbsp;
to manufacture dozens if not hundreds of these new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.640
costumes, which were much more intricate than the&nbsp;
stormtrooper outfits created for the first film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:04.080
The idea of Super Troopers was scrapped, but the&nbsp;
design was undeniably great and a new, individual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.280
character was conceived to wear it — the bounty&nbsp;
hunter Boba Fett. The costume was given some color&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.560
and some wear to give it a sense of history and&nbsp;
to distinguish it from proper Imperial attire.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.560
Like "Sith" or "Palpatine," the words&nbsp;
"Mandalore" and "Mandalorian" are never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.120
uttered in the original trilogy, but fans came to&nbsp;
know it and associate it with the armor through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.240
the wealth of ancillary material released about&nbsp;
the film universe throughout the 1980s and '90s.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.960
"You may take Captain Solo to Jabba&nbsp;
the Hutt after I have Skywalker."

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.360
"He's no good to me dead."

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.520
The fact that Boba Fett says and does very&nbsp;
little in his first two film appearances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.840
did nothing to dampen fan enthusiasm to&nbsp;
learn more about him and the origin of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.240
his slick armor. The original Star Wars&nbsp;
Expanded Universe — comprised of novels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:55.360
comics, video games, and tabletop RPG sourcebooks&nbsp;
published between 1978 and 2014 — offered an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.600
enormous amount of information about the bounty&nbsp;
hunter and the culture from which he hails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.760
the Mandalorians. Their homeworld of&nbsp;
Mandalore became the setting of many stories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.400
and home to an army of characters wearing&nbsp;
variations on the beloved costume design.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.080
Mandalore is established to be a&nbsp;
planet on the Outer Rim of the galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.160
and the namesake of an entire sector of&nbsp;
space. A temperate, Earth-like world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:21.360
Mandalore is notable for being the exclusive home&nbsp;
of a near-indestructible metal called beskar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.480
from which its resident warrior&nbsp;
culture constructs their armor.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.520
The Mandalorian religion demands war and conquest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:32.000
and Mandalore becomes the seat of an&nbsp;
expanding empire during the Old Republic era,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.720
thousands of years before the Skywalker Saga.&nbsp;
This leads to war against the Sith, the Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.200
the Republic, and frequently themselves,&nbsp;
as Mandalore lacks a central government.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.000
In the year 738 BBY, the Jedi and&nbsp;
Republic resolve to preempt the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.680
threat of Mandalorian expansion&nbsp;
by bombarding their core worlds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.160
including Mandalore itself. The Mandalorian&nbsp;
Excision leaves their empire in ruins.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.480
By the time of the Clone Wars, the&nbsp;
surface of Mandalore is a barren desert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.200
its remaining cities are&nbsp;
housed beneath giant domes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.200
and generations of resentment still exists&nbsp;
between the Mandalorians and the Jedi.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.840
However, this may not have always been the case,&nbsp;
as at least one Mandalorian served the Jedi Order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.080
a thousand years earlier, around the height&nbsp;
of the Old Republic. This Mandalorian Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.040
named Tarre Vizsla, invents a unique lightsaber&nbsp;
called the Darksaber that becomes a legendary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:24.480
totem — a sort of Mandalorian Excalibur. After&nbsp;
Tarre Viszla's death, the Darksaber is entombed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.280
at the Jedi Temple on Coruscant, but is later&nbsp;
"liberated" by his descendants and returned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.240
Mandalore, where for generations its wielder&nbsp;
commands the respect of all Mandalorian clans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.080
The blade is either passed down through&nbsp;
inheritance or won through single combat.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.960
While there is only one Darksaber, traditional&nbsp;
armor is also built specifically to mimic or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.720
counter the abilities of the Jedi:&nbsp;
its repulsors mimic a Force Push&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.160
while its flamethrower is difficult&nbsp;
for Jedi to parry with a lightsaber.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:55.280
The beskar used to create this armor is, likewise,&nbsp;
passed down and recast across generations.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.320
A generation before the Clone Wars break out&nbsp;
across the galaxy, Mandalore is wrenched by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.600
civil war of its own, devastating the population.&nbsp;
When the war is over, a peace movement builds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:10.640
momentum across the planet, leading to the birth&nbsp;
of a new pacifist government. Mandalorians who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.520
still wish to follow their warrior tradition are&nbsp;
exiled from the planet to its moon, Concordia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:20.080
where they rally behind the Darksaber and form&nbsp;
a rogue fighting force called Death Watch.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:25.760
The pacifist New Mandalorians are led by Duchess&nbsp;
Satine Kryze and appointed Prime Minister Almec,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.800
whose reforms reshape Mandalore into a society&nbsp;
more closely resembling that of peaceful and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:34.400
prosperous worlds in the core of the&nbsp;
Galactic Republic. When war breaks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.800
out between the Republic and the Confederacy&nbsp;
of Independent Systems, Satine insists that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.040
Mandalore remain neutral, and becomes the&nbsp;
leader of the Council of Neutral Systems.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.200
"As the designated regent of 1500 systems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:52.640
I speak for thousands of worlds that have urged&nbsp;
me to allow them to stay neutral in this war."

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:56.960
This decision allows the New Mandalorians to&nbsp;
remain pacifist, but it also ends up costing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.040
them in other ways, as it strains her&nbsp;
diplomatic relationship with the Republic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:05.760
nearly to its breaking point, and both sides in&nbsp;
the Clone Wars bar Mandalorians from using their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.400
space lanes for trade. The public is forced to&nbsp;
rely on an expensive black market for goods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:15.040
a practice for which Prime Minister Almec is&nbsp;
eventually arrested and removed from office.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:21.120
The Death Watch's leader, Pre Vizsla, sees the&nbsp;
new, pacifist Mandalore as weak and disgraceful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:26.160
and seeks a way to return to the homeworld and&nbsp;
seize power. However, Death Watch's ranks are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:30.400
thin and Satine is a popular leader.&nbsp;
Vizsla finds an ally in Count Dooku,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:34.160
leader of the Coalition of Independent&nbsp;
Systems, and they hatch a plot to turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.320
the public against Satine and open the door&nbsp;
for his triumphant return to Mandalore.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:43.520
Dooku and Vizsla arrange a bombing on Mandalore,&nbsp;
prompting Satine and visiting Jedi Obi-Wan Kenobi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:48.160
to investigate. They discover that Death Watch&nbsp;
is behind the bombing and that the CIS may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.080
be involved, which prompts the Republic&nbsp;
Senate to consider installing a military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.840
presence on Mandalore — against Satine's&nbsp;
will — in order to keep the planet out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:00.720
of Separatist hands. This is all part of&nbsp;
Dooku's plan, since a Republic occupation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:03.840
would be enormously unpopular&nbsp;
among the Mandalorian public.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.080
Death Watch would return to rid the planet&nbsp;
of the invaders, throw Satine under the bus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:10.560
and take charge with the&nbsp;
full support of the people.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:15.920
Satine, Kenobi, Anakin Skywalker, and Padmé&nbsp;
Amidala manage to unravel this plan and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:19.440
dissuade the Senate from approving&nbsp;
this invasion. After this failure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:24.560
Count Dooku cuts ties with Pre Vizsla and Death&nbsp;
Watch retreats deeper into the Mandalorian sector.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.200
During their travels across space, Death&nbsp;
Watch happens upon a craft carrying two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:34.320
wounded passengers — former Sith apprentice Maul&nbsp;
and his own charge and brother, Savage Opress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:39.200
Like Vizsla, Maul hates the Jedi and holds a&nbsp;
bitter grudge against Obi-Wan Kenobi. Sensing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:44.320
an opportunity, Vizsla invites Maul to team up&nbsp;
and retake Mandalore, which would provide Maul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:49.400
an opportunity to take revenge on Kenobi. Maul&nbsp;
accepts, and formulates a plan similar to Dooku's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:54.240
— arrange for a massive crime wave on Mandalore&nbsp;
that is beyond Duchess Satine's peacekeepers'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:58.960
capacity to repel, therefore allowing&nbsp;
Death Watch to return as conquering heroes.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.680
Pre Vizsla endorses the plan, offering Death&nbsp;
Watch as muscle to force the galaxy's three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.360
biggest crime syndicates to cooperate.&nbsp;
The scheme goes off without a hitch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.120
as the crime wave turns the public&nbsp;
against Satine's pacifist leadership&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:15.520
and gives Pre Vizsla the opening he needs&nbsp;
to clean up the mess and win their support.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.320
"Death Watch is here to save&nbsp;
you from these intergalactic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.800
gangsters that threaten our great city."

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.160
Once he's thrown Satine in jail&nbsp;
and taken the throne for himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:29.520
Vizsla attempts to dispose of Maul and Opress,&nbsp;
but finds he's underestimated them — Maul always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:34.320
planned to consolidate the syndicates and to use&nbsp;
Mandalore as the seat of his new criminal empire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:39.200
and to him, it's Vizsla who's outlived his&nbsp;
usefulness. Maul kills Viszla in ritual combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:43.280
winning the Darksaber, leadership of&nbsp;
Death Watch, and the Mandalorian throne.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.240
Maul keeps his newfound power&nbsp;
a secret from the public,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.800
reinstalling Almec as his puppet Prime Minister.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:52.720
While much of Death Watch falls&nbsp;
in line behind their new leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:57.280
Pre Vizsla's lieutenant Bo-Katan&nbsp;
Kryze efuses to follow an outsider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:02.960
and leads a splinter group against Maul. Bo-Katan&nbsp;
springs her sister Duchess Satine from prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:08.400
who in turn summons her star-crossed lover Obi-Wan&nbsp;
Kenobi to Mandalore. This, too, plays into Maul's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:13.840
hands, as it affords him the opportunity to&nbsp;
kill Satine in front of Kenobi, simultaneously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:19.440
eliminating a political rival and punishing his&nbsp;
Jedi arch-nemesis. The attempt to quickly remove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:24.720
Maul from power is unsuccessful, and Kenobi and&nbsp;
Bo-Katan's squad are forced to flee Mandalore.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:29.280
Months later, Bo-Katan convinces the Jedi&nbsp;
Council to lend her a battalion to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:35.520
her unseat Maul as ruler of Mandalore. Aided by&nbsp;
clone Commander Rex, ex-Jedi advisor Ahsoka Tano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.360
and a segment of the 501st Legion, Bo-Katan's&nbsp;
remaining loyal warriors lay siege to the capital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:47.120
city of Sundari. They are met by Maul's Death&nbsp;
Watch, led by Gar Saxon of House Vizsla. Ahsoka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:52.000
Tano captures Maul after a hard-fought lightsaber&nbsp;
duel, while Bo-Katan easily takes the throne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:56.960
room from relative pushover Almec. With their&nbsp;
leadership removed and their forces overwhelmed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:02.240
the combined might of Bo-Katan's Mandalorians and&nbsp;
the Republic's clones, Maul's forces surrender.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:06.960
The Republic names Bo-Katan the new Regent&nbsp;
of Mandalore, nominally granting the planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:11.680
the self-determination they crave as they escape&nbsp;
from under the boot of Maul's Shadow Collective.

00:09:12.636 --> 00:09:17.120
The Siege of Mandalore ends mere days before the&nbsp;
fall of the Republic and its reformation into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:21.680
the Galactic Empire, which quickly shatters&nbsp;
any illusions of Mandalorian independence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:26.880
When Bo-Katan refuses to follow Emperor&nbsp;
Palpatine's orders, she is stripped of her regency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:32.720
and replaced by a new Imperial Governor — Maul's&nbsp;
former right hand, Gar Saxon. Saxon creates a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:37.760
army of Mandalorian Super Commandos, repurposing&nbsp;
the armor and traditions of Death Watch to serve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:42.880
the Empire and to punish any Mandalorian clan&nbsp;
that doesn't fall in line behind the new order.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:46.960
One group of warriors, the Protectors, is&nbsp;
permitted to go about their own affairs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:51.200
carry on Mandalorian traditions, as long as&nbsp;
they are in tune with Imperial interests.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.960
"Why would I fight the Empire when&nbsp;
obviously destroying you is so much easier?"

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.560
When they're discovered allowing the Rebel&nbsp;
Alliance to use their hyperspace lanes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.400
the entire clan is wiped out.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.280
Mandalore also plays host to an Imperial Academy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:08.240
which not only trains stormtroopers and potential&nbsp;
Super Commandos, but also conducts research and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:13.440
development for new weapons and technology. One&nbsp;
Academy student, Sabine Wren, develops a weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:18.080
called the Arc Pulse Generator, which fires&nbsp;
bursts of energy that seek out beskar armor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:23.040
superheating it and incinerating anyone inside,&nbsp;
while leaving any other combatants totally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:27.440
untouched. Eager to prove her brilliance,&nbsp;
Sabine builds a working prototype, but when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:32.320
she realizes that the Empire might actually&nbsp;
use it against Mandalorians, she destroys it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:36.880
and leaves Mandalore to become a bounty hunter&nbsp;
and, eventually, a leader in the Rebel Alliance.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:41.200
Mandalore spends nearly two decades&nbsp;
tightly under Imperial rule,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:46.240
its once-proud clans brought to heel by Gar&nbsp;
Saxon and his Super Commandos. Saxon makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:51.120
an example of Clan Wren after Sabine's defection&nbsp;
— Sabine's father is imprisoned and her brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:56.240
Tristan is conscripted into the Super Commandos&nbsp;
in order to assure Clan Wren's cooperation.

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:59.840
"How can you wear that armor,&nbsp;
Tristan? How could you join them?"

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.560
"You shouldn't have come back, Sabine."

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.880
Meanwhile, Sabine herself has been fighting&nbsp;
the Empire as a member of Phoenix Squadron.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:11.920
During their travels, her team happens across the&nbsp;
Darksaber, which has been missing for decades.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:16.720
Sabine learns to wield the saber as a weapon,&nbsp;
but feels ill-suited to use it for its symbolic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:21.280
purpose — to rally all Mandalorians to her&nbsp;
command. She brings the weapon back to her mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:26.160
Ursa Wren's home on Krownest in the hopes of&nbsp;
recruiting Clan Wren into the Rebel Alliance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:30.480
Gar Saxon intervenes, but he is&nbsp;
defeated in single combat by Sabine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:33.520
and then killed by Ursa before&nbsp;
he can shoot Sabine in the back.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.160
Clan Wren begins to openly oppose the Empire,&nbsp;
which brings other clans to their aid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:43.360
including Clan Kryze, still led by Bo-Katan.&nbsp;
Together with Sabine's Jedi friends Ezra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:47.920
Bridger and Kanan Jarrus, Clans Wren and&nbsp;
Kryze return to Mandalore and defeat a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:52.640
plot by its new Imperial Governor — Gar's&nbsp;
brother Tiber Saxon — to use Sabine's Arc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:57.920
Pulse Generator against Mandalore. After this&nbsp;
victory, Bo-Katan accepts the Darksaber and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:02.480
a number of clans pledge loyalty to her and&nbsp;
her fight to free Mandalore from the Empire.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:07.200
Little is yet known about the fate of Mandalore&nbsp;
after the start of Bo-Katan's rebellion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:11.760
but it does not appear to have gone well. A&nbsp;
decade after the clans unite to oppose the Empire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:16.160
Mandalorians have been all but wiped out after&nbsp;
an event referred to as "The Great Purge,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:21.200
during which the Empire slaughtered countless&nbsp;
Mandalorians and forced the remainder into hiding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:25.840
The Mandalorian's first season reveals that a&nbsp;
small tribe of Mandalorians live in secret on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:30.320
the planet Navarro, leaving their underground&nbsp;
home only one at a time in order to hide their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:34.080
numbers — or perhaps, lack thereof. This tribe,&nbsp;
which may be one of many, practices a much more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:39.280
strict form of the Mandalorian religion than that&nbsp;
demonstrated by other Mandalorians seen to date,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.688 --> 00:12:43.600
not permitted to reveal their names or even&nbsp;
remove their helmets except in private.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.360
"This is the way."

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:49.520
Further evidence of the damage to Mandalore&nbsp;
and its people is the Empire's raiding of its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:55.040
prized resources. Officers of the now-fallen&nbsp;
Empire now possess large quantities of beskar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.960
stolen from either fallen warriors or the&nbsp;
planet itself, which they sell back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:03.600
Mandalorians in exchange for their service as&nbsp;
bounty hunters. As seen in the season 1 finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:06.800
the Darksaber itself has landed&nbsp;
in the possession of Moff Gideon.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:12.320
During the second season of The Mandalorian,&nbsp;
Mando's quest to return the Child to his people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:16.800
leads him to Trask, a watery moon where he and&nbsp;
the Child almost meet their doom before they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:21.920
saved by a trio of Mandalorians led by Bo-Katan.&nbsp;
Mando is shocked when his saviors immediately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:26.080
doff their helmets, revealing themselves to be&nbsp;
adherents of a very different sort of creed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.600
but they're able to set aside their&nbsp;
disagreements long enough to make a deal:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:34.080
If he helps them raid an ex-Imperial ship and&nbsp;
steal weaponry, they'll put him on the right path&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.640
toward a Jedi who can potentially train the Child.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:40.880
Mando's new allies have more in mind for the raid&nbsp;
than they're letting on, of course — as Bo-Katan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:45.120
reveals when she accosts the ship's commander and&nbsp;
demands to know where Moff Gideon's holding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:49.600
artifact she needs to claim her rightful place&nbsp;
at the Mandalorian throne. But the commander&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:54.400
kills himself before he can be forced to reveal&nbsp;
any information. It's a disappointing setback,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:59.040
although with Gideon hunting Mando and Bo-Katan&nbsp;
searching for Gideon, it's more than likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:03.840
their paths will cross again — and reveal more&nbsp;
about the history and current fate of Mandalore.

